<section id="A1.SS6" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.6 </span>Data Visualization</h3>

<section id="A1.SS6.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">A.6.1 </span>GUI Understanding</h4>

<div id="A1.SS6.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS6.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To qualitatively demonstrate our data in GUI understanding tasks, we provide examples that cover both element-level and screenshot-level understanding.
At the element level, we have designed five distinct tasks regarding individual GUI elements. Table <a href="#A1.T16" title="Table 16 ‣ A.6.1 GUI Understanding ‣ A.6 Data Visualization ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ ScaleCUA: Scaling Open-Source Computer Use Agents with Cross-Platform Data" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a> showcases specific examples of these tasks.
At the screenshot level, we focus on the ability to comprehend the entire GUI interface globally and its dynamic changes. Table <a href="#A1.T17" title="Table 17 ‣ A.6.1 GUI Understanding ‣ A.6 Data Visualization ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ ScaleCUA: Scaling Open-Source Computer Use Agents with Cross-Platform Data" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">17</span></a> provides examples for these two tasks.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A1.T16" class="ltx_table">
